# Cline Rules — ElectroScheme Studio

Work in patch mode only.

Project root: G:\electroscheme-studio
Patch folder: C:\1
Product: ElectroScheme Studio
Repository: electroscheme-studio
Stack: Python/FastAPI backend + Vue/Vite/TypeScript frontend

Token economy:
- Do not inspect the whole repo when a few files are enough.
- Do not print full files unless requested.
- Do not repeat known context.
- Do not propose multiple architectures unless asked.
- Prefer one safe implementation.
- Keep responses short: Done / Checks / Status / Next.

Patch rules:
- All changes go through numbered PowerShell patches.
- Patch name: patch_XXX_short_description.ps1
- Repair name: patch_XXX_repairN_short_description.ps1
- Use one log only: _logs\<patch>_<timestamp>.transcript.log
- Start every patch with Start-Transcript.
- Always close transcript in finally.
- A small _patches\<patch>.applied.json marker is allowed.
- Do not create extra summary .log files.

PowerShell rules:
- Target Windows PowerShell 5.1.
- Do not use PowerShell 7-only syntax.
- Never write source/config files with Set-Content -Encoding UTF8.
- Write JSON/TS/Vue/CSS/HTML/Python/TOML/MD as UTF-8 without BOM using System.Text.UTF8Encoding($false).
- Capture stdout/stderr of important native commands with Start-Process.
- Do not let expected failures like missing origin remote crash the patch.

Git/GitHub:
- Branch: main.
- Repo: https://github.com/genrudko/electroscheme-studio
- Commit only after checks pass.
- Keep commits small.
- Use HTTPS origin if SSH host key is not configured.
- If pushing workflows, gh token needs workflow scope.

Checks before commit:
- Backend: install requirements and direct smoke-test health/demo_project.
- Frontend: npm install and npm run build.
- Keep npm run typecheck separate; do not block early MVP bootstrap on strict typecheck if Vite build passes.

Scope:
- Make minimal changes.
- Do not change project name, stack, or architecture without request.
- Do not add DWG/CAD/cloud/multi-user features now.
- Do not add large dependencies without reason.
- Do not reformat unrelated files.

Repair patches:
- Minimal repair only.
- State root cause in patch header.
- Re-run failed check.
- Improve logging if the previous error was hidden.

Product boundary:
- Local-first WebUI editor for interactive electrical schemes.
- Early focus: model, SVG renderer, selection, properties, terminals/connections, validation, export later.